what is ER Diagram?
An ER Diagram is used in database Management System to design and visualize a database structure.

There are three types
1. Entity     2. Attribute    3. Relationship/mapping/caridinality


Entity:- An Entity is an object.It reprsented as rectangle in ER Diagram.

Entity are 2 types   
1. strong Entity         2. weak Entity

Weak Entity:- an Entity that cannot be unqualiy dentified by its own attribute and define upon another entity is called weak entity.It is representd as double-rectangle. 

Attribute:- An attribute is an property of the entity. It is reprsented by ellipse.

There are four types
1. key   2. Multivalue    3. dervide   4. composite

key attribute:-  A key attribute can unquely , identity an entity from an Er diagram. it reprsented as ______.

Multivalue attribute:- An attribute that can hold Multivalue is known as Multivalue attribute.It is reprsented by double ellipse.

Derived attribute:- An attribute that us derived from another attribute is known as derived attribute.It is reprsented by dash ellipse.

composite attribute:- An attributeis the combination of multiple attributeis known as composite attribute, It is representd by Dashed ellipse.

Mapping :- caridinality define the numerical attribute of the Relationship between two entity.

There are four types
1. one to one    2. one to many  3. many to one   4. Many to Many

one to one :- when a single instance of an entity is asscoiated with single instance of another entity then is called onr to one Relationship.
example:-

one to many :- when a single instance of an entity is asscoiated with more than one instance of another entity then it is called many to one Relationship.  
example:-
Many to one:- when more than one instance of an entity are associated with a single instance of another entity, then it is called many to one Relationship.
example:-
Many to many:- when more than one instance of an entity are associated with more than  instance of another entity, then it is called many to many Relationship.

